course: dictionary
lesson: 2434
title: Daddy, and words with more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so you need the words around them to find the right one. «She asks Daddy to make a noise.» Here Daddy is a name for a father, because a little girl is talking to her dad.
explain: Daddy is an informal word, the kind you use with family and friends. It is what young children call their father, and older children usually say Dad.
explain: Now look at «the daddy of them all». Daddy means something different here: it is slang for the biggest or best one. Ask yourself: is this a father, or something big and important? The clues in the sentence tell you which.
fact: Daddy is a noun, and its plural is daddies.
fact: «Daddy» (informal) means what young children call their father.
fact: «Daddy» (slang) in «the daddy of them all» means the biggest or best one.
fact: Older children usually say Dad rather than Daddy.
fact: The harvestman, or daddy longlegs, is not a spider: it has a one-piece round body, two eyes, no silk and no venom.
exercise: «She asks Daddy to make a noise.» Who is Daddy in this sentence? | A water-tank | A bear in a picture book | A spider in the garden | *Her father
exercise: Mia says «the daddy of them all» means her dad. What does daddy mean here? | *The biggest or best one | An old bucket | A small animal with long legs | A grown-up who is someone's dad
exercise: What is the plural of daddy? | *daddies | daddys | daddyes | daddy's
test: What is a harvestman, or daddy longlegs? | A spider that spins silk | A kind of father | *An arachnid that is not a spider | A water-tank on a hill
test: Which word do older children usually say for their father? | Pa | Papa | *Dad | Daddy
exam: Which sentence uses daddy as slang? | Taffy fills the tank, and Daddy is pleased. | Her Daddy pulls her left ear. | *The race was the daddy of them all. | She asks Daddy to make a noise.
